# Prospect cron-redirected logs. Installed by deploy/deploy-scripts.sh into
# /etc/logrotate.d/prospect (system logrotate runs it daily from /etc/cron.daily).
#
# WHY copytruncate on ALL of these: every one is written by a shell `>> file 2>&1` redirect
# (crontab lines) or an `exec >>$LOG` inside a script (prospect-refresh.sh) — the writing
# process keeps its fd open for the whole job (up to 6h for the nightly) and none of them
# understands a "reopen your log" signal, so rename-and-recreate rotation would send hours of
# output to a file logrotate already moved away. copytruncate never loses a writer. Its one
# quirk — a copy+truncate race can drop the few lines written between the two — is worth
# far less than losing a nightly's ETL tail, the exact line that explains a failed build.
#
# The dated per-step logs (/var/log/prospect-steps/<step>.<timestamp>.log) are deliberately
# NOT rotated here: prospect-refresh.sh and quiet-window.sh write one file per run and
# prospect-refresh.sh prunes them itself (find -mtime +14 -delete), and a running step's
# live log must never be truncated under its writer. Only the *.cron.log files in that
# directory are append-forever.
#
# /var/log/prospect-backup.log joined when the 19:30 backup was re-enabled (2026-09-01;
# see deploy/crontab.txt's history block) — it had been growing unbounded on the schedule
# entry's redirect ever since the job first ran.

/var/log/prospect-refresh.log
/var/log/prospect-alerts.log
/var/log/prospect-cron-wrap.log
/var/log/prospect-backup.log
/root/deepen_backfill.log
/root/dev_socials_keeper.log
/var/log/prospect-steps/*.cron.log
{
    weekly
    rotate 4
    compress
    delaycompress
    missingok
    notifempty
    copytruncate
}
